      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Plunging is a technique that requires a good seal; you need to get the cup of the plunger completely submerged in the water in the sink. Then, you plunge vigorously up and down, creating a strong suction and pressure change to dislodge the clog. You can't easily check the pipe underneath without some tools, but if you have a small drain inspection camera or even a flashlight and a small scope, you might get a peek. If you're worried about the pipe, be careful not to force anything if the clog is deep, as you don't want to cause a bigger mess.",
